Z||000001||GREENDANO||07-04-99||06:43 AM||||Sorry it Sucks Anyways....<br>  Actually I think it's Pontiac's equivalent to the Camaro RS of that generation (3rd), also a V6.  The Pontiac just has the nicer interior, IMHO.  It was just a basic car with a basic motor so people could be driving a "sports car" with-out spending a ton of money.  Hey, that sort-of sounds like our cars.  At least Fieros can  carry a little speed with them.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000002||GREENDANO||07-04-99||01:07 PM||||Here's an update from the Pontiac desk....<br>  I talked to my buddy today about the SSA.<br>  You should feel pretty good.  He tells me the SSA was the aniversary TA that had the Grand National 3.8 with the turbo.  So V6 yes, but with big power.  My guess, he wasn't messing with you.  That car is as fast as any well equiped v-8 street car.  <br>  Dan-O
